{"id": "swebq0003", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The language spoken by Serb people is Serbian. It belongs to the South Slavic group of languages and is closely related to Croatian, Bos nian, and Montene grian. These language s are often considered part of a single family called Ser bian-Croat ian-Bosnian-Montene grian, though they have distinct regional variations in dialects and spelling conventions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "swebq0011", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "swebq0019", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Egyptians speak Egyptian Arabic, which is a dialect of the Arab ic language. It has its own unique features and vocabulary that differ from other forms of Arab ic spoken across the region.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "swebq0027", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Malaysia is a federal parliamentary constitutional monarchy. The king, or the Yang di-Pert hujaan Agong in Malay, serves as head of state and is elected by an assembly of state rulers for a five- year term. The actual governing power rests with the prime minister, who leads the cabinet and is chosen from among members of parliament based on majority support. The country has a bicameral parliament made up of the Dewan R enang Negara, or Senate, which has 7 0 members appointed for fixed terms, and the Dewan Rakyat, or House of Representatives, which consists of 2 22 elected members. While the monarch holds ceremonial role s, the executive branch, led by the prime minister, handles day-to-day governance alongside legislative functions shared between the two houses.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 44, "carrier_ended": null}
