{"id": "swebq0043", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Steinbeck was influenced to start writing by his experiences growing up in Sal ina, California, and the social issues he observed during the Great Depression. He often wrote about the lives of ordinary people, especially farm ers and migrant workers, which deep ened his commitment to storytelling as a way to highlight human struggle and resilience.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
