{"id": "swebq0123", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Ptolemy was a Greek scholar who lived in Alexandria around the 2nd century AD. He wrote about astronomy, geography, and math, but he's best known for his work on the geocentric model of the universe, which placed Earth at the center with everything else revolving around it. His ideas were widely accepted for centuries until they were challenged by later scientists like Copernicus.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "swebq0131", "pool": "swebq", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Isaac Newton was a brilliant scientist who helped us understand the laws of motion and gravity. He figured out how things move and why objects fall to the ground, which changed science forever.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
